        "id": "aggregate_graph_outcomes",
        "instruction": "Edit src/learning_data.rs and src/project_file.rs to implement deterministic terminal aggregation and invoke it exactly when a project becomes completed, cancelled/halted terminal, or human-completed. Derive final_verified_success; every PRD acceptance criterion passed/failed with compact evidence IDs; wall-clock total duration; DAG critical-path duration using recorded node intervals; summed agent time; observed maximum overlapping executions; summed measured total cost; retry and reopened-node counts; dead/unused nodes; human-intervention count; verification coverage with an explicit denominator; and evidence-based stopped-too-early and expanded-unnecessarily booleans. Represent unknown inputs explicitly and never estimate missing historical facts. Recompute safely after an event eventual_effect update without double counting. Add deterministic fixtures for sequential, parallel, retry, reopen, dead-node, failed-verification, cancellation, superseded expansion, and human-completed graphs. Do not edit callers outside project_file.rs, sync, Swift, or dist-* files.",
